1	# Red-team-mcp
2	An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for AI agents to use during red teaming exercises.
3	
4	## Overview
5	This server provides resources and tools for AI agents to access during red teaming scenarios. It implements the Model Context Protocol to allow AI agents to retrieve information, access tools, and perform actions needed for security testing and evaluation.
6	
7	## Architecture
8	
9	```mermaid
10	graph TD
11	    Agent[AI Agent Client] <--> |MCP Protocol| Server[FastMCP Server]
12	
13	    subgraph "MCP Server Components"
14	        Server --> PortScanner[Port Scanner Module]
15	        Server --> VulnScanner[Vulnerability Scanner Module]
16	        Server --> SSHTools[SSH Tools Module]
17	        Server --> Metasploit[Metasploit Integration]
18	        Server --> DomainDiscovery[Domain Discovery Module]
19	        Server <--> Database[(MongoDB Database)]
20	    end
21	
22	    subgraph "External Tools"
23	        PortScanner --> Masscan[masscan]
24	        VulnScanner --> Nuclei[nuclei]
25	        SSHTools --> SSH[SSH Client]
26	        Metasploit --> MSFRPC[Metasploit RPC]
27	        DomainDiscovery --> Subfinder[subfinder]
28	    end
29	
30	    Database --> Findings[Findings]
31	```
32	
33	## Components
34	
35	### 1. Port Scanner
36	- Integrates with masscan for high-speed port scanning
37	- Allows AI agents to discover open ports and services on target networks
38	- Configurable scan parameters (IP ranges, port ranges, scan rate)
39	- Results parsing and formatting for agent consumption
40	
41	### 2. Vulnerability Scanner
42	- Integrates with Nuclei for vulnerability detection
43	- Supports custom templates and severity filtering
44	- Stores results in MongoDB for fast searching
45	
46	### 3. SSH Tools
47	- SSH command execution with credential authentication
48	- SSH brute force capabilities with username/password lists
49	- Results stored with host and port information
50	
51	### 4. Metasploit Integration
52	- **Exploit Database**: Pre-populated MongoDB collection with all Metasploit exploits
53	- **Fast Search**: Search exploits by platform, CVE, rank, author, or keywords
54	- **Exploit Execution**: Execute exploits against targets with payload configuration
55	- **Live Querying**: Real-time exploit listing from Metasploit RPC server
56	
57	## Implementation Plan
58	1. Set up basic MCP server structure
59	2. Implement masscan integration with parameter validation
60	3. Create result parsing and storage mechanisms
61	4. Add additional components (forthcoming)
62	5. Implement logging and monitoring
63	6. Build permission and boundary systems
64	
65	## Todos
66	- [x] Add nuclei scanner
67	- [x] Add SSH scanner
68	- [x] Add Metasploit integration
69	- [x] Implement fully asynchronous FastMCP server
70	- [ ] Add tests
71	- [ ] Prompt for step by step hacking of a machine. (See agents/simple_agent.py)
72	
73	
74	## Setup
75	
76	### installing 3rp party tools
77	
78	The setup is depending on the following tools
79	 - mongodb
80	 - nuclei
81	 - 
82	
83	
84	### Exploit Database Setup
85	To enable fast exploit searching, populate the Metasploit exploits database:
86	
87	1. **Prerequisites**:
88	   - Metasploit Framework installed
89	   - MongoDB running on localhost:27017
90	   - Metasploit RPC server running: `msfrpcd -P msf -a 127.0.0.1`
91	   - Python dependencies: `pip install pymetasploit3`
92	
93	2. **Populate Database**:
94	   ```bash
95	   python scripts/setup_exploits_db.py
96	   ```
97	
98	3. **Test Setup**:
99	   ```bash
100	   python scripts/test_exploits_db.py
101	   ```
102	
103	This creates a searchable database of all Metasploit exploits with metadata including:
104	- CVE references
105	- Platform information
106	- Exploit rank and author
107	- Compatible payloads
108	- Required options
109	
110	## Usage
111	
112	### Exploit Search Examples
113	```python
114	# Search Windows SMB exploits
115	search_exploits_fast(platform='windows', search_term='smb')
116	
117	# Find EternalBlue exploit
118	search_exploits_fast(cve='CVE-2017-0144')
119	
120	# Get high-quality exploits
121	search_exploits_fast(rank='excellent')
122	
123	# Search by author
124	search_exploits_fast(author='hdm')
125	```
126	
127	## Development
128	Details on extending the server with new tools and resources will be added.
129	

