1	# TickTick MCP
2	
3	A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that provides tools for integrating TickTick task management tools. Using Python and the MCP SDK.
4	
5	## Overview
6	
7	This repository contains a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server implementation for TickTick. It provides a standardized way for AI assistants and applications to interact with TickTick's task management functionality, allowing operations like:
8	
9	- Retrieving projects and tasks
10	- Creating new projects and tasks
11	- Updating task details
12	- Completing and deleting tasks
13	
14	With this MCP, AI systems can act as task masters to help manage your to-do lists and tasks in TickTick with natural language.
15	
16	## Requirements
17	
18	- Python 3.8+
19	- TickTick account
20	- TickTick API key (via OAuth) # COMMENT: I will add a tool to generate an API key from the TickTick developer portal
21	
22	## Installation
23	
24	1. Clone this repository
25	
26	   ```bash
27	   git clone https://github.com/ekkyarmandi/ticktick-mcp.git
28	   cd ticktick-mcp
29	   ```
30	
31	2. Install dependencies
32	
33	   ```bash
34	   pip install -r requirements.txt
35	   ```
36	
37	## Obtaining a TickTick API Key
38	
39	This MCP uses TickTick's OpenAPI scheme, which requires registering an app through TickTick's developer portal:
40	
41	1. Go to the [TickTick Developer Documentation](https://developer.ticktick.com/docs)
42	2. Click on `Manage Apps` in the top right corner and login with your TickTick credentials
43	3. Register a new app by clicking the `+App Name` button
44	4. Enter a name for your app (only required field)
45	5. Once created, you'll be able to see your `Client ID` and `Client Secret`
46	6. For the `OAuth Redirect URL`, enter a URL where you'll be redirected after authorization (e.g., `http://127.0.0.1:8080`)
47	
48	### Authorizing Your App
49	
50	After registering your app, use the [ticktick-py](https://github.com/lazeroffmichael/ticktick-py) library to get your access token:
51	
52	```python
53	from ticktick.oauth2 import OAuth2
54	
55	# Replace with your details from the developer portal
56	client_id = "YOUR_CLIENT_ID"
57	client_secret = "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET"
58	redirect_uri = "YOUR_REDIRECT_URI"  # e.g., http://127.0.0.1:8080
59	
60	auth_client = OAuth2(client_id=client_id,
61	                    client_secret=client_secret,
62	                    redirect_uri=redirect_uri)
63	
64	# This will open a web browser for authorization
65	# Follow the instructions in the terminal to authorize
66	auth_client.get_access_token()
67	```
68	
69	After authorizing, the access token will be saved to a `.token-oauth` file by default. You can extract the token from this file or use:
70	
71	```python
72	print(auth_client.token_info["access_token"])
73	```
74	
75	## Configuration
76	
77	1. Create a `.env` file in the root directory with your TickTick API key:
78	   ```
79	   TICKTICK_API_KEY=your_access_token_here
80	   ```
81	
82	## Usage
83	
84	Run the MCP server:
85	
86	```bash
87	python main.py
88	```
89	
90	This will start the MCP server on port 8000. You can now connect to it using any MCP client.
91	
92	### Available Tools
93	
94	The server provides the following tools:
95	
96	- `get_projects`: Get a list of all projects
97	- `project_details`: Get details of a specific project
98	- `get_task_details`: Get details of a specific task
99	- `create_project`: Create a new project
100	- `create_task`: Create a new task in a project
101	- `update_task`: Update an existing task
102	- `complete_task`: Mark a task as complete
103	- `delete_task`: Delete a task
104	
105	### Example Interactions
106	
107	Once your MCP server is running, AI systems can help manage your tasks with natural language commands like:
108	
109	- "Show me all my projects"
110	- "Create a new project called 'Home Renovation'"
111	- "Add a task to buy groceries tomorrow"
112	- "Mark my 'Pay bills' task as complete"
113	- "What tasks do I have due this week?"
114	- "Delete the task about the canceled meeting"
115	
116	## Using with MCP Clients
117	
118	This server can be used with any MCP-compatible client, such as:
119	
120	- Claude Desktop
121	- Cursor IDE
122	- Custom AI applications using MCP SDKs
123	
124	## Development
125	
126	To extend or modify this MCP server:
127	
128	1. Add new tools in `tools.py`
129	2. Register them in `main.py` using `mcp.add_tool()`
130	
131	## License
132	
133	MIT
134	
135	## Contributing
136	
137	Contributions are welcome! Please feel free to submit a Pull Request.
138	

