## 2. File Contents

### `main.py`

```python
from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP
from mcp.server.sse import SseServerTransport
from starlette.applications import Starlette
from starlette.routing import Mount, Route

from tools import *

mcp = FastMCP("ticktick_mcp")

mcp.add_tool(get_projects)
mcp.add_tool(project_details)
mcp.add_tool(get_today_tasks)
mcp.add_tool(get_task_details)
mcp.add_tool(create_project)
mcp.add_tool(create_task)
mcp.add_tool(update_task)
mcp.add_tool(complete_task)
mcp.add_tool(delete_task)

tp = SseServerTransport("/messages/")

async def handle_sse(request):
    async with tp.connect_sse(request.scope, request.receive, request._send) as streams:
        await mcp._mcp_server.run(
            streams[0], streams[1],
            mcp._mcp_server.create_initialization_options(),
        )

routes = [
    Route("/sse", endpoint=handle_sse),
    Mount("/messages/", app=tp.handle_post_message),
]

app = Starlette(routes=routes)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    import uvicorn
    uvicorn.run(app, host="0.0.0.0", port=58321)
```

### `config.py`

```python
from decouple import config

TICKTICK_API_BASE = "https://api.ticktick.com/open/v1"
TICKTICK_API_KEY = config("TICKTICK_API_KEY")
HEADERS = {
    "Authorization": f"Bearer {TICKTICK_API_KEY}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
}
```

### `tools.py`

Defines 8 async MCP tools (decorated with `@mcp.tool()`), all calling `https://api.ticktick.com/open/v1` via `httpx.AsyncClient`:

| Tool | HTTP Method | Endpoint |
|---|---|---|
| `get_projects()` | GET | `/project` |
| `project_details(project_id)` | GET | `/project/{id}/data` |
| `get_today_tasks(timezone="Asia/Jakarta")` | Multiple GETs | iterates all projects |
| `get_task_details(project_id, task_id)` | GET | `/project/{pid}/task/{tid}` |
| `create_project(project_name)` | POST | `/project` |
| `create_task(...)` | POST | `/task` |
| `update_task(...)` | POST | `/task/{tid}` |
| `complete_task(project_id, task_id)` | POST | `/project/{pid}/task/{tid}/complete` |
| `delete_task(project_id, task_id)` | DELETE | `/project/{pid}/task/{tid}` |

### `auth.py`

A standalone script to obtain an OAuth2 token via the `ticktick.oauth2.OAuth2` class. Not imported by `main.py`. Uses a `YOUR_CLIENT_ID` / `YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET` placeholder flow and prints `auth_client.access_token_info`.

### `requirements.txt`

Lists 29 pinned packages (see dependency list below).

