489	    """
490	    Get search guidance and resolve search query errors
491	
492	    Args:
493	        ctx: FastMCP Context
494	
495	    Returns:
496	        Detailed guidance on mail search properties, valid formats, and troubleshooting tips for search errors
497	    """
498	    return """
499	Available email search properties:
500	
501	1. subject - The text in the subject line of an email
502	   Example: {"subject": "meeting"}
503	
504	2. body - The content in the body of an email
505	   Example: {"body": "project update"}
506	
507	3. from_email - The sender of an email (name or address)
508	   Example: {"from_email": "john.doe@example.com"}
509	
510	4. to_email - The direct recipient of an email
511	   Example: {"to_email": "jane"}
512	
513	5. cc_email - Recipients copied on the email
514	   Example: {"cc_email": "team"}
515	
516	6. has_attachments - Whether the email has attachments (true/false)
517	   Example: {"has_attachments": true}
518	
519	7. is_read - Whether the email has been read (true/false)
520	   Example: {"is_read": false}
521	
522	8. folder_id - The ID of the folder to search in (default: inbox)
523	   Example: {"folder_id": "AQMkADAwATM0MDAAMS1hM"}
524	
525	9. count - The maximum number of results to return (default: 20)
526	   Example: {"count": 50}
527	
528	You can combine multiple properties in a single search:
529	Example: {"from_email": "john", "has_attachments": true, "is_read": false, "count": 10}
530	
531	To use these properties, create a JSON object with your desired search criteria and pass it to the advanced_mail_search tool.
532	"""
